\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}
%=============================================================================

\ours{} demonstrates that geometric collision awareness can be internalized directly into VLA flow-matching weights through SDF auxiliary supervision, producing a policy whose standard forward pass generates collision-aware actions with zero runtime overhead. Unlike inference-time methods that introduce auxiliary modules (SDF servers, constraint solvers, depth pipelines), \ours{} requires only the same RGB observations as the base VLA, reducing the safety-critical path to a single forward pass.

